From f81cd5346a88065a0fedc034e23013bb881cb9d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tavis Rudd <tavis@damnsimple.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2026 08:35:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Introduce ReaderT-based CfnM monad for CFN operation
 threading

Replace explicit 6-parameter threading (CfnContext, env name,
RemoteImports, emit callback, StackArgs, argsfile path) with a
ReaderT CfnEnv IO monad. Session-scoped read-only context (CfnContext,
environment name, RemoteImports, emitter) lives in CfnEnv; per-operation
data (StackArgs, Maybe FilePath) stays as explicit parameters.

Converted: all Tier 1 operations (createStack, updateStack,
createOrUpdate, createChangeset, estimateCost, lintTemplate,
templateApprovalRequest), RequestBuilder build functions, and the
Runner callback type. Tier 2 operations (deleteStack, watchStack,
describeStack, etc.) remain in IO for now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
